 **Parameters:**
-- $C_{cool}$: Typical values are blues or cyans (e.g., $(0.0, 0.0, 1.0)$).
-- $C_{warm}$: Typical values are reds, oranges, or yellows (e.g., $(1.0, 0.5, 0.0)$).
-- Reference vector: View direction or Light direction.
+- $C_{cool}$ and $C_{warm}$ define the color temperature range (e.g., blue to red) [S2][S4, unofficial].
+- Reference vector determines whether shading is light-relative or view-relative [S2][S3, unofficial].
 
